subject: fix(memory): make toolPruner truncation idempotent

PR #3599 review (§6) reproduced non-idempotent truncation in
open-sse/services/memory/toolPruner.js: pruning the same already-truncated
output again re-truncates (591→589 chars in probe) because the truncation
notice itself gets cut on subsequent passes. Since the pipeline re-runs over
stored history every request, repeated passes degrade historical tool outputs.

Fix: truncateText now detects the '[... Tool output truncated by 9router
memory optimizer:' marker and skips re-truncation (no-op, savedChars=0),
so once-truncated output is stable under any later pass, even if
maxHistoricalChars is lowered between passes.

Tests (tests/unit/memory-enhancements.test.js, toolPruner section):
- preserves recent tool turns and truncates older ones (PR original)
- regression: prune(twice) === prune(once) — byte-identical, no re-cut
- marker-bearing content never re-truncated even over budget

Verified: node --test tests/unit/memory-enhancements.test.js → 3/3 pass;
review probe: first pass 591 chars, second pass pruned=false 591 chars.

